# The whole project's behaviour, written as expectations. Each directory is a section of the
# docs (a leading 01- only orders it), and a section's Background is the setup everything in
# it starts from, on top of its parent's. See .claude/skills/writing-specs for how to write them.
#
#   cargo run -p expectation_cli -- check expectations              check it (no window)
#   cargo run --release -- --expect --docs docs                     run the sim's tests, write docs/
#   cargo run -p expectation_cli -- docs expectations docs          rewrite docs/ from saved results

Suite: T1-S Ranger
  This is a flight simulator for the HEEWING T1-S Ranger, a small plane with two motors that
  you throw by hand. It also has a ground control station that flies the plane with
  ArduPilot.

  Start with [[The simulator]]. There, you throw the plane and fly it from the keyboard.
  Then use the [[Ground control station]] to plan missions and fly them. The ground control
  station runs ArduPlane on the physics of the sim.

# Both systems fly the same plane, so they share its state.
Vocabulary:
  # The screen of the TX15 (the aviation tests and the station's tests on the serial line)
  State: the TX15 screen mode is MANUAL | FBWA | AUTO | RTL | QHOVER | QLOITER | CRUISE | QRTL
    Set: let ArduPilot fly this mode
    Shows: {value}: the first lamp on the screen of the TX15 shows this flight mode
  State: the TX15 screen arming is armed | disarmed
    Set: arm or disarm the plane
    Shows: armed: the second lamp on the screen of the TX15 shows ARMED, and it is amber
    Shows: disarmed: the second lamp on the screen of the TX15 shows DISARMED, and it is dark
  State: the plane is in hand | being carried back | launching | flying | on the ground | crashed | flying the mission | flying home | loitering
    Shows: in hand: the plane is in your hand at the pilot box
    Shows: being carried back: the HUD says "Bringing it back to your hand..."
    Shows: launching: the throw starts, and the plane leaves your hand when time runs again
    Shows: flying: the plane leaves your hand and climbs away
    Shows: on the ground: the plane lands and stops on the ground
    Shows: crashed: the plane hits the ground, and the HUD says CRASHED with the reason and "Press R to reset"
    Shows: flying the mission: the plane climbs and flies to the first waypoint
    Shows: flying home: the plane turns for home
    Shows: loitering: the plane circles the last item
